<title>TAIWAN: YAGEO JAN-JULY SALES UP 24 PCT YR/YR.</title>
<headline>YAGEO JAN-JULY SALES UP 24 PCT YR/YR.</headline>
<dateline>TAIPEI 1997-08-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Taiwan's leading resistor maker Yageo Corp said on Monday its January-July sales rose 24 percent to T$1.483 billion from T$1.196 billion in the same period in 1996.</p>
<p>In July alone, its sales hit a monthly record of T$236 million, up 23 percent from T$191 million in July 1996, Yageo said in a statement.</p>
<p>Yageo said the company's sales were expected to grow in the second half of 1997 due to rising orders.</p>
